WEBVTT

00:03.980 --> 00:08.270
Mother... In Barcelona, I met a wonderful pair of lovers.

00:09.230 --> 00:13.110
I wonder what kind of love you and father experienced a long time ago.

00:13.910 --> 00:16.120
If we ever meet, please tell me about it, okay?

00:26.420 --> 00:27.710
NAAJA

00:26.420 --> 00:27.710
Nadja,

00:27.840 --> 00:30.380
With your eyes

00:27.840 --> 00:30.380
Kimi no hitomi ni wa

00:30.380 --> 00:31.590
Nadja,

00:30.380 --> 00:31.590
NAAJA

00:31.630 --> 00:33.880
What do you see?

00:31.630 --> 00:33.880
Nani ga mieru

00:33.930 --> 00:36.800
Shining in the far distance,

00:33.930 --> 00:36.800
Haruka tooku hikaru

00:36.800 --> 00:39.180
The door to the future,

00:36.800 --> 00:39.180
Mirai no tobira

00:40.100 --> 00:43.560
That's what I'm searching for

00:40.100 --> 00:43.560
Sagashite iru

00:43.560 --> 00:50.780
Tomorrow's Nadja

00:51.480 --> 00:54.990
If everyone could meet with a smile

00:51.480 --> 00:54.990
Minna egao de aetara

00:55.070 --> 00:58.320
I'm sure there would be no more fighting

00:55.070 --> 00:58.320
Arasoi mo kitto nakunaru

00:58.370 --> 01:01.580
It could be so much more fun

00:58.370 --> 01:01.580
Konna ni mo tanoshi kunaru

01:01.620 --> 01:05.040
The world is wide, but it's still one

01:01.620 --> 01:05.040
Sekai wa hiroi kedo hitotsu ne

01:05.420 --> 01:08.710
I can't see the end of the journey

01:05.420 --> 01:08.710
Tabi no owari wa mienai

01:08.840 --> 01:12.170
God is the only one who could possibly know

01:08.840 --> 01:12.170
Kamisama ga tabun shitteru

01:12.340 --> 01:15.930
To the people who, someday, I will meet again

01:12.340 --> 01:15.930
Itsukamata deaeru hito tachi ni

01:15.970 --> 01:18.090
I will go waving

01:15.970 --> 01:18.090
Te wo furinagara

01:18.180 --> 01:24.850
Sometimes, there are days I feel blue,

01:18.180 --> 01:24.850
Toki ni wa BURUU ni naru hi mo aru kedo

01:24.890 --> 01:27.600
But I won't look back

01:24.890 --> 01:27.600
Ushiro mukanai

01:27.940 --> 01:32.900
Until the day my dream comes true

01:27.940 --> 01:32.900
Yume ga kanau hi made

01:33.190 --> 01:36.610
Nadja, Your smile

01:33.190 --> 01:36.610
NAAJA kimi no hohoemi wa

01:36.700 --> 01:40.030
Nadja, gives me courage

01:36.700 --> 01:40.030
NAAJA yuuki ni naru

01:40.070 --> 01:42.990
Under the blue sky,

01:40.070 --> 01:42.990
Aoi sora no shita de

01:43.120 --> 01:45.960
I will find the place

01:43.120 --> 01:45.960
Ashita no yukue

01:46.250 --> 01:50.170
where my future lies

01:46.250 --> 01:50.170
Mitsukeru kara

02:09.250 --> 02:09.920
﻿The Black...

02:09.920 --> 02:10.630
﻿It's the Black Rose!

02:10.610 --> 02:12.750
﻿The Black Rose has appeared!

02:32.440 --> 02:36.280
﻿Granada! Oh, ancient capital of Spain!

02:36.900 --> 02:38.900
﻿Hey, Kennosuke! From now on....

02:38.900 --> 02:39.610
﻿Siesta..

02:42.570 --> 02:43.530
﻿Hey, everyone!

02:43.530 --> 02:46.990
﻿Siesta.

02:52.270 --> 02:53.400
What's wrong with you guys?

02:53.400 --> 02:54.650
Saying "Siesta, Siesta."

02:54.670 --> 02:56.670
﻿They're talking about taking an afternoon nap, Nadja.

02:57.420 --> 02:59.420
﻿It's the custom for people around this area.

02:59.550 --> 03:01.470
﻿Because it's so hot, they take an afternoon nap.

03:02.050 --> 03:04.640
﻿No way! Even though the weather is this nice outside?

03:04.640 --> 03:05.890
﻿According to the newspaper,

03:05.890 --> 03:08.850
﻿today's forecasted temperature for Granada will be 50 degrees Celsius.

03:08.980 --> 03:12.190
﻿For us foreigners, we won't even feel like moving.

03:12.690 --> 03:15.310
﻿If you're going out, walk in the shade as much as possible.

03:18.610 --> 03:20.610
﻿The Black Rose will appear in Granada.

03:25.830 --> 03:28.040
﻿So the Black Rose will be in this town too.

03:33.250 --> 03:34.500
﻿What's wrong, Nadja?

03:41.380 --> 03:44.010
﻿There really isn't a single person around.

03:53.690 --> 03:56.860
﻿You must never part with this brooch.

03:58.820 --> 03:59.820
﻿Francis...

04:00.860 --> 04:03.240
﻿I wonder what you're doing right now.

04:07.240 --> 04:08.830
﻿That's dangerous... little lady.

04:09.410 --> 04:10.950
﻿Watch where you're going when you walk!

04:11.160 --> 04:12.370
﻿I'm sorry!

04:17.590 --> 04:18.380
﻿Huh?

04:19.460 --> 04:20.630
﻿My brooch is gone!

04:21.170 --> 04:21.880
﻿No way!

04:25.470 --> 04:28.100
﻿Thief! Wait!

04:29.510 --> 04:30.680
﻿Tourists..

04:31.020 --> 04:32.640
﻿...shouldn't just stand around looking dazed!

04:32.770 --> 04:33.850
﻿What the heck!

04:34.480 --> 04:37.100
﻿I don't want to hear that from a thief like you!

04:37.900 --> 04:39.650
﻿Huh? What?

04:42.860 --> 04:44.030
﻿My mother's...

04:44.240 --> 04:46.160
﻿My mother's precious brooch is...

04:55.330 --> 04:56.460
﻿What's with you?

04:56.460 --> 04:57.750
﻿Move it!

04:59.000 --> 05:00.500
﻿I told you to move it, didn't I?

05:01.300 --> 05:02.210
﻿Why you...

05:07.590 --> 05:10.100
﻿Second-rate pickpockets... Go away!

05:13.430 --> 05:14.430
﻿I told you, didn't I?

05:14.730 --> 05:17.980
﻿You must never part with this brooch.

05:19.820 --> 05:21.440
﻿Y-You're...

05:23.070 --> 05:24.190
﻿Francis!

05:25.280 --> 05:29.160
﻿No My starry... eyed... knight!

05:35.060 --> 05:40.060
﻿The Other Side of Francis

05:41.290 --> 05:44.800
﻿You must never part with this brooch.

05:45.920 --> 05:47.470
﻿You remembered, didn't you?

05:48.640 --> 05:49.470
﻿Remember?

05:50.220 --> 05:52.560
I ﻿mean, on the night of that ball...

05:52.810 --> 05:55.140
﻿How you saved me at Applefield that time...

05:55.730 --> 05:57.560
﻿You didn't seem to remember that.

05:59.980 --> 06:00.940
﻿I really wanted to see you.

06:01.690 --> 06:04.360
﻿Whenever I’ve thought about seeing you, I have.

06:04.780 --> 06:06.650
﻿It's like a miracle!

06:06.990 --> 06:08.360
﻿A blessing from God...

06:09.070 --> 06:10.950
﻿No, it's definitely fate!

06:12.450 --> 06:14.950
﻿Fate... huh?

06:28.470 --> 06:30.090
﻿How wonderful this is!

06:30.470 --> 06:32.300
﻿Things like this do actually happen, don't they?

06:32.800 --> 06:34.720
﻿Even though Europe is so big.

06:35.310 --> 06:39.100
﻿On top of that, our meeting wasn't even planned. What a coincidence...

06:39.310 --> 06:41.100
﻿To think I'd run into you again...

06:44.690 --> 06:47.230
﻿Like those five occurrences that happened after I joined the troupe...

06:47.490 --> 06:49.490
﻿In an unknown town, meeting someone you know unexpectedly...

06:49.780 --> 06:52.280
﻿It's quite an amazing coincidence, but it seems to happen a lot!

06:52.990 --> 06:55.370
﻿By the way, do you like siestas?

06:55.830 --> 06:57.910
﻿I hate siestas.

06:58.080 --> 07:02.750
﻿I mean, I think it's a waste of time taking an afternoon nap when the weather's this nice.

07:03.040 --> 07:06.800
﻿In the first place, I don't really understand people who take afternoon naps.

07:07.420 --> 07:08.460
Do you understand?

07:08.840 --> 07:09.420
﻿I'm not sure.

07:10.220 --> 07:12.970
﻿At the orphanage, there were a lot of children that were smaller than me.

07:13.090 --> 07:16.680
﻿It was my duty to comfort the crying and complaining children.

07:16.970 --> 07:19.810
﻿That's why I actually haven't taken many afternoon naps.

07:20.310 --> 07:23.270
﻿That's right! On the other hand, nights are amazing!

07:23.440 --> 07:26.320
﻿After praying and getting into bed, they were asleep in five seconds.

07:27.190 --> 07:29.400
﻿But it seemed like they could never find a good sleeping position to sleep in.

07:29.650 --> 07:32.070
﻿When they woke up in the mornings, everyone was always in such a mess.

07:32.070 --> 07:33.490
﻿It was always like that.

07:34.030 --> 07:35.660
﻿Do you have a good sleeping position you sleep in?

07:36.200 --> 07:37.030
﻿Probably bad too, I suppose.

07:37.740 --> 07:40.410
﻿Between sunny weather and rainy weather, which one do you like?

07:40.520 --> 07:41.080
Sunny.

07:41.080 --> 07:42.330
﻿I like sunny weather too!

07:42.870 --> 07:46.290
﻿If it's sunny in the morning, it's really a happy feeling, isn't it?

07:46.650 --> 07:47.440
It is.

07:48.170 --> 07:51.510
﻿Hmm... but I like cloudy and rainy days too.

07:51.800 --> 07:53.510
﻿I like all the various kinds of weather!

07:53.800 --> 07:56.100
﻿I like it when the raining clouds show frightening menace.

07:56.350 --> 07:59.350
And also, I like the rainbow that ﻿stays after the storm has passed.

07:59.470 --> 08:01.560
﻿By the way, what about the seasons?

08:01.560 --> 08:02.230
﻿Summer.

08:02.350 --> 08:03.730
﻿I like summer too!

08:03.900 --> 08:06.360
I ﻿mean, the flowers are so beautiful!

08:07.480 --> 08:08.570
﻿But, I like winter too!

08:08.730 --> 08:09.940
﻿I like all of them!

08:10.440 --> 08:12.490
﻿I also like going down and stepping all the way through that snow packed on the ground-.

08:12.820 --> 08:14.610
﻿And even when I can't see the daybreak because of the fog...

08:14.910 --> 08:15.660
﻿By the way...

08:17.910 --> 08:19.660
﻿Am I too loud?

08:21.080 --> 08:21.660
﻿Not at all.

08:22.080 --> 08:23.250
﻿I'm too loud, aren't I?

08:24.330 --> 08:24.920
﻿Why?

08:25.710 --> 08:28.170
﻿How much you talk is just right...

08:28.170 --> 08:30.210
﻿compared to bashful, refined young ladies that hold themselves back.

08:33.590 --> 08:34.800
﻿You know, my mother...

08:35.430 --> 08:37.550
﻿while dreaming of seeing the outside world...

08:37.930 --> 08:40.220
﻿died in the end without setting a single foot outside.

08:42.060 --> 08:44.020
﻿You're different though, aren't you?

08:47.980 --> 08:51.360
﻿Now that you mention it, I've been wondering ever since before.

08:51.820 --> 08:52.400
﻿What is it?

08:52.940 --> 08:56.320
﻿It feels like you're different somehow from your normal self.

08:56.320 --> 08:57.320
﻿I'm not different.

08:57.530 --> 08:58.240
﻿I wonder if that's true.

08:58.620 --> 08:59.280
﻿It's true.

09:03.410 --> 09:05.660
﻿I'm always like this.

09:08.770 --> 09:09.730
I'm sorry.

09:10.460 --> 09:15.550
﻿Being apart for a while,. I was worried that maybe something changed.

09:16.510 --> 09:18.180
﻿That's all I was feeling.

09:18.720 --> 09:20.390
﻿So don't worry about it.

09:20.680 --> 09:21.560
﻿Francis.

09:31.980 --> 09:33.070
﻿But...

09:34.150 --> 09:35.110
﻿After all...

09:39.530 --> 09:42.280
﻿It feels like you're not... your usual self.

09:53.760 --> 09:54.510
﻿Nadja.

09:57.340 --> 09:58.800
﻿You've stopped talking all of a sudden.

09:59.640 --> 10:01.350
No, not really.

10:01.600 --> 10:03.890
﻿I bet you talked so much that you're thirsty.

10:06.180 --> 10:06.770
﻿Look.

10:33.210 --> 10:33.920
﻿Tomatoes.

10:35.000 --> 10:35.550
﻿Eat up.

10:40.590 --> 10:41.590
﻿Now that you mention it,

10:42.350 --> 10:43.760
﻿when I was at the orphanage,

10:44.720 --> 10:47.430
﻿didn't the farmer's wife give us tomatoes?

10:48.560 --> 10:50.440
﻿Wiping them with our sleeves, we ate them together.

10:51.440 --> 10:52.150
﻿But...

10:52.900 --> 10:57.150
﻿I would never have thought that I'd receive a tomato from Francis.

11:00.160 --> 11:03.200
﻿Was Francis... this kind of person?

11:17.550 --> 11:18.800
﻿It's good!

11:19.420 --> 11:23.090
﻿It's good, isn't it? Right? It's really good!

11:25.850 --> 11:27.470
﻿This is really delicious!

11:28.730 --> 11:30.390
﻿It's really, really good.

11:45.740 --> 11:47.870
Watching someone's face while eating,

11:48.120 --> 11:49.240
﻿doesn't that make it hard to eat?

11:49.540 --> 11:50.750
﻿Really?

11:51.080 --> 11:52.460
I'm pretty much okay with it.

11:53.330 --> 11:55.750
﻿I'm an expert at doing two things at once.

11:56.380 --> 12:00.300
﻿Also, I want to watch you while you eat a tomato.

12:00.510 --> 12:03.260
﻿Is my munching on a tomato really that mysterious?

12:03.300 --> 12:04.680
﻿Yeah! Mysterious!

12:05.600 --> 12:08.220
﻿I mean, it's because you're a nobleman.

12:08.810 --> 12:11.100
﻿I thought you guys never ate like this.

12:11.430 --> 12:12.940
﻿So it's a new discovery?

12:13.140 --> 12:14.190
﻿For me...

12:14.850 --> 12:17.480
﻿It feels like I've discovered a new aspect of you.

12:18.070 --> 12:19.440
﻿That's why I'm happy!

12:51.220 --> 12:54.180
﻿By the way, do you know about this palace?

12:55.400 --> 12:57.350
﻿I don't really know all the details, but...

12:58.020 --> 12:59.650
﻿If that's the case, I'll tell you about it.

13:00.070 --> 13:02.190
﻿I studied pretty hard on this.

13:04.110 --> 13:06.530
﻿This palace, called the Alhambra Palace...

13:06.740 --> 13:08.820
﻿was made a really long time ago.

13:09.030 --> 13:10.240
﻿The thirteenth century.

13:10.830 --> 13:14.580
﻿To be precise, construction began in the year 1230.

13:15.160 --> 13:16.960
﻿Uh... ah... and so...

13:17.170 --> 13:20.290
﻿The people that built it were of the governing body that reigned in the Iberian peninsula.

13:20.300 --> 13:21.670
﻿The Islamic King was...

13:21.670 --> 13:23.920
﻿Muhammed I of the Nasrid Dynasty, wasn't it?

13:24.550 --> 13:26.840
﻿From there, with the advent of many great kings,

13:26.840 --> 13:30.050
﻿it slowly came to completion over a span of 170 years.

13:31.010 --> 13:32.930
﻿Uh, a-after that...

13:33.060 --> 13:34.430
﻿Reco... Renco... Recon..

13:34.430 --> 13:35.350
﻿Reconquista.

13:35.890 --> 13:38.480
﻿Due to the Christian reconquest of the country,

13:38.770 --> 13:42.190
﻿the Islamic people and their king were driven out of the Iberian peninsula.

13:42.980 --> 13:45.190
﻿Leaving behind this beautiful palace as it is.

13:48.820 --> 13:51.490
﻿However, the true beauty of this palace...

13:51.780 --> 13:55.290
﻿doesn't lie within it's elaborate arabesque artwork, or it's beautiful landscape gardening.

13:56.460 --> 13:58.210
﻿To come from behind with a great victory...

13:58.330 --> 14:00.000
﻿They trifled with fate.

14:00.840 --> 14:03.630
﻿It truly lies in the courage and gallant people who fought for it.

15:58.870 --> 15:59.910
﻿That's dangerous.

16:00.250 --> 16:01.910
﻿Ah, I was so surprised! Haha!

16:02.120 --> 16:04.500
﻿I'm sorry! I guess I was being just a bit too high-spirited!

16:11.510 --> 16:12.880
﻿There's something inside.

16:17.890 --> 16:18.930
﻿A kaleidoscope.

16:19.640 --> 16:20.640
﻿A kaleidoscope?

16:21.850 --> 16:23.140
﻿Take a look inside.

16:27.360 --> 16:28.610
﻿It's so beautiful!

16:30.530 --> 16:32.860
﻿This is so amazing! It's so mysterious!

16:36.450 --> 16:38.490
﻿The world is sparkling!

16:40.080 --> 16:42.200
﻿That's... a memento of my mother.

16:42.580 --> 16:44.040
﻿Eh? This is?

16:44.960 --> 16:47.000
﻿Withering in the shade of the forest called nobility.

16:47.460 --> 16:49.790
﻿For my mother, who never went into the outside world,

16:50.250 --> 16:54.550
﻿that kaleidoscope was her one and only window to see the world.

16:55.680 --> 16:56.720
﻿My poor mother.

16:58.350 --> 16:59.970
﻿However, this is what I think.

17:01.180 --> 17:04.140
﻿In reality, instead of through that kaleidoscope,

17:04.480 --> 17:07.650
﻿I'm positive that she was thinking that she wanted to see the world with her own eyes.

17:08.730 --> 17:09.400
﻿That's right.

17:10.230 --> 17:11.940
﻿For example, like you...

17:14.200 --> 17:16.280
﻿I wonder... if you'd take that.

17:17.820 --> 17:19.570
﻿For... my mother.

17:23.120 --> 17:24.200
﻿Francis...

17:29.540 --> 17:32.300
﻿Once again, I can see a new side of you.

18:00.780 --> 18:01.950
﻿Francis.

18:04.830 --> 18:07.160
﻿Who... are you?

18:10.960 --> 18:12.040
﻿Why are you..

18:12.550 --> 18:15.420
﻿showing me a different side of yourself every time we meet?

18:16.420 --> 18:17.510
﻿Why?

18:18.050 --> 18:19.590
﻿I don't understand why, but...

18:20.050 --> 18:22.350
﻿Somehow, it's just... incredibly painful...

18:24.350 --> 18:24.930
﻿Nadja.

18:25.730 --> 18:27.480
﻿I want you to remember at least this much.

18:28.600 --> 18:29.350
﻿I am me.

18:30.100 --> 18:31.350
﻿I am no one else.

18:32.860 --> 18:33.480
﻿And also...

18:35.480 --> 18:37.820
﻿The feelings that you're experiencing now are...

18:38.280 --> 18:40.200
﻿without a doubt, feelings meant for me.

18:41.990 --> 18:42.780
﻿That much...

18:44.450 --> 18:46.290
﻿I really want you to remember.

18:48.210 --> 18:49.040
﻿I...

18:49.830 --> 18:50.870
﻿I...

18:51.130 --> 18:54.880
﻿I don't understand why you seem like you're in such pain.

18:55.710 --> 18:58.340
﻿If you don't mind, please talk to me about it.

18:58.630 --> 19:01.260
﻿If there's anything I can do... Francis!

19:53.730 --> 19:54.730
﻿I...

19:57.190 --> 19:58.440
﻿I like you.

20:01.240 --> 20:02.820
﻿From the moment I first met you,

20:04.030 --> 20:05.780
﻿I've liked you so much that it's unbearable.

20:07.490 --> 20:08.160
﻿But...

20:08.580 --> 20:09.870
﻿meeting you today,

20:09.870 --> 20:13.500
﻿having come to know so many different aspects of you that I didn't know about until now,

20:14.630 --> 20:15.750
﻿I've grown to...

20:16.790 --> 20:18.670
﻿like you even more.

20:24.050 --> 20:26.640
﻿I... like how you are today.

20:27.260 --> 20:29.390
﻿I like all of you even more than before.

20:34.190 --> 20:34.890
﻿Nadja.

20:36.270 --> 20:37.020
﻿What is it?

20:38.550 --> 20:39.340
I...

20:41.070 --> 20:41.860
﻿I...

20:42.280 --> 20:43.280
﻿I'm really...

20:51.410 --> 20:54.080
﻿Well then, let's meet again somewhere.

20:55.170 --> 20:56.120
﻿Uh... Wait!

21:13.180 --> 21:13.890
﻿That's...!

21:14.640 --> 21:15.640
﻿Francis?!

21:21.690 --> 21:23.900
﻿There are two... Francis's?

21:24.110 --> 21:26.650
﻿Just what's... going on here?!

21:29.370 --> 21:30.410
﻿Nadja.

21:30.870 --> 21:32.740
﻿I want you to remember at least this much.

21:33.540 --> 21:36.460
I ﻿am me. I am no one else.

21:36.870 --> 21:39.000
﻿The... The Black Rose!

21:40.040 --> 21:40.960
﻿And also...

21:41.710 --> 21:46.090
﻿The feelings that you're experiencing now are, without a doubt, feelings meant for me.

21:51.390 --> 21:55.100
﻿I... like how you are today.

21:59.060 --> 22:02.360
﻿I like all of you even more than before.

22:03.280 --> 22:04.530
﻿I like you.

22:05.150 --> 22:06.530
﻿I like you.

22:14.470 --> 22:17.720
Paris is sunnier than London

22:14.470 --> 22:17.720
RONDON don yori haretara PARI

22:17.840 --> 22:20.930
Carmen likes paella more than pasta

22:17.840 --> 22:20.930
CARUMEN men yori PAERIYA suki

22:21.350 --> 22:27.520
The Queen of Spades is a fickle person

22:21.350 --> 22:27.520
SUPEEDO no jou kimagure yasan

22:28.480 --> 22:29.720
Indeed

22:28.480 --> 22:29.720
Kitto

22:32.480 --> 22:34.900
It's not use worrying about it

22:32.480 --> 22:34.900
Nayan datte MUDA yo

22:35.480 --> 22:38.610
Que sera sera, sera Sera

22:35.480 --> 22:38.610
KE SERA SERA SERA SERA

22:38.870 --> 22:43.580
Tomorrow's going to be whatever it was meant

22:38.870 --> 22:43.580
Ashita nante itsumo naru you ni

22:43.660 --> 22:45.040
To be, to be

22:43.660 --> 22:45.040
Naru naru

22:45.370 --> 22:50.380
The tree fog won

22:45.370 --> 22:50.380
Sekai KAERU tobi KONKUURU

22:50.840 --> 22:54.760
The world frog-jumping contest

22:50.840 --> 22:54.760
Yuushou shita yo AMAGAERU

22:57.970 --> 23:04.140
Under the kitten's paw

22:57.970 --> 23:04.140
Koneko chan no ashi no ura wa

23:04.560 --> 23:10.730
Is the scent of the sun, right?

23:04.560 --> 23:10.730
Otentou sama no nioi dane

23:13.570 --> 23:16.900
Paris is sunnier than London

23:13.570 --> 23:16.900
RONDON don yori haretara PARI

23:16.990 --> 23:19.990
Carmen likes paella more than pasta

23:16.990 --> 23:19.990
CARUMEN men yori PAERIYA suki

23:20.490 --> 23:26.870
It's not the time to hang around

23:20.490 --> 23:26.870
Michikusa shite iru baai ja nai ne

23:27.750 --> 23:32.250
Indeed, indeed

23:27.750 --> 23:32.250
Kitto kitto

23:40.600 --> 23:41.320
Tomorrow's Nadja

23:41.460 --> 23:43.750
﻿Kennosuke is like a sunflower.

23:44.210 --> 23:45.880
﻿Always, always so straight-forward and upright.

23:46.210 --> 23:48.500
﻿The spirit of the samurai, was it?

23:49.130 --> 23:50.130
﻿Now that you mention it,

23:50.130 --> 23:53.430
﻿what was Kennosuke aiming for when he came all the way to Europe?

23:54.430 --> 23:55.970
﻿Kennosuke's dream?

23:56.140 --> 23:57.510
﻿Was it to fly in the sky...?

23:58.020 --> 23:59.430
﻿Eh? Am I wrong?

23:59.640 --> 24:03.020
﻿Kennosuke’s dream is much, much bigger!

24:03.690 --> 24:06.110
Tomorrow's Nadja. The High-Flying Kennosuke.

24:04.250 --> 24:07.210
The High-Flying Kennosuke!

24:06.270 --> 24:08.150
﻿Now, the door of destiny opens.
